note OM-1 TWIN of unroll-nest-64x2.om for the pinned compiler 734f0a39: same expectation.
note Contract section 4 lines 87-92, 110 and erratum E7: the 64-copy limit is per unrolled loop, so an unroll 2
note nested in an unroll 64 (128 copies of the inner body) is accepted; the total is bounded only by the
note 65536-word limit. Removing unroll (twin unroll-nest-64x2-rolled.om) changes nothing.
note Expected stdout: oracle/s3s4/exp/unroll-nest-64x2.out (python3, oracle/s3s4/oracle.py).
note OM-1 unit: this line replaces the om2 line
fn main to int
f = ulong 1
c = ulong 0
for i ulong 64
for j ulong 2
f = add mul f 31 add mul i 2 j
c = add c 1
end
end
pu f
pu c
ret 0
end
